WEBVTT

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:08.130
Are you okay, Ashiya?

00:00:08.340 --> 00:00:10.800
I apologize, Sire.

00:00:11.010 --> 00:00:13.510
I'm so wretched I can't even do the shopping...

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:17.220
Whatever, just behave yourself and stay in bed. I'll make dinner.

00:00:17.430 --> 00:00:23.600
Sire! Oh, such kind words... for such a hopeless servant...

00:00:23.810 --> 00:00:27.480
We've got some rice left, so maybe I'll make porridge with egg.

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:29.570
Is that Emi again?

00:00:29.780 --> 00:00:30.740
Special delivery!

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:34.780
Y-You bastard... You ordered something behind my back again...

00:00:34.990 --> 00:00:39.490
Nope. And if I did, I'd have 'em deliver it while you weren't here.

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:41.410
Have a nice day!

00:00:44.250 --> 00:00:47.340
"I've found lots of wonderful things in Hawaii,

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:52.380
so would you sell them for me at the
Neighborhood Association's summer bazaar?"

00:00:54.800 --> 00:00:56.050
FYI, I won't help.

00:00:56.260 --> 00:00:58.010
You--!

00:01:00.010 --> 00:01:03.980
Hey, either complain or cough!
One or the other!

00:01:04.190 --> 00:01:05.770
Y--!

00:01:07.110 --> 00:01:08.440
You're...

00:01:08.650 --> 00:01:11.400
You're with the Church, yes?

00:01:11.610 --> 00:01:14.990
"Deathscythe Bel," if I recall correctly.

00:01:26.330 --> 00:01:30.630
<i>Right here, this moment,</i> <i>this is our starting point</i>

00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:36.630
<i>Let's picture what we might be able to do</i>

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:40.680
<i>Unbelievable things can happen sometimes</i>

00:01:40.890 --> 00:01:46.390
<i>More... we can push past this</i>

00:01:47.940 --> 00:01:57.280
<i>Everything is born from zero;</i>
<i>I want to shine, flap my wings hard</i>

00:01:58.530 --> 00:02:01.740
<i>And fly to that sky</i>

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:08.920
<i>Come on, let's go, with</i> <i>brilliant smiles on our faces!</i>

00:02:09.130 --> 00:02:14.710
<i>Let's fly off to an unknown world right now</i>

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:19.300
<i>I decide, I'm the one who chooses my future</i>

00:02:19.510 --> 00:02:21.680
<i>Let's follow our dreams</i>

00:02:21.890 --> 00:02:23.220
<i>Sure, some days we'll cry</i>

00:02:23.430 --> 00:02:29.600
<i>It's a precious wish, don't disappear</i>

00:02:29.810 --> 00:02:37.530
<i>I'm going after the future you,</i> <i>because I know I'll find you</i>

00:02:57.050 --> 00:03:02.550
Tom's shop has been closed for days. Is he sick or somethin'?

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:07.730
That guy was always defying the Grand Hoshin Church, you know?

00:03:07.930 --> 00:03:10.400
Word is, he even gave the federation of knights priority

00:03:10.600 --> 00:03:12.110
when he passed out food and supplies.

00:03:12.310 --> 00:03:13.940
So he's gonna face the Inquisition?!

00:03:14.150 --> 00:03:18.360
Keep it down, you idiot!
What if they overheard us?!

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:27.040
I've been informed that Lucifer's army is invading Porridge village.

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:31.420
Isn't a platoon of Church knights stationed there?

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:35.380
How about we send reinforcements, and then they'll owe us one?

00:03:35.590 --> 00:03:39.920
Nah, it wouldn't make a difference.
The enemy force is too big.

00:03:40.130 --> 00:03:44.260
Which means the smart play is to pretend we never heard about it.

00:03:44.470 --> 00:03:46.850
Aha, your idea is to tell the world

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:49.980
about how the Church knights failed to protect the village,

00:03:50.180 --> 00:03:54.730
and then have our federation take the initiative in subduing Satan?

00:03:54.940 --> 00:04:01.740
Eh, it's not like sacrificing one little village really affects us!

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.320
Who goes there?!

00:04:05.370 --> 00:04:06.450
H-Hey!

00:04:06.660 --> 00:04:07.830
What's wrong?!

00:04:09.250 --> 00:04:10.790
Did the wine have--?!

00:04:18.920 --> 00:04:22.800
Are you with the Inquisition, you wench?!

00:04:23.010 --> 00:04:24.430
Dammit--

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:34.940
You... Church lapdog!

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:39.280
St-Stop!

00:04:47.240 --> 00:04:53.040
Well done. Your work was as efficient as always. I'm impressed.

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:54.920
Wipe the blood off.

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:59.550
Some of the blame for the inability of our knights and theirs

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:04.130
to band together against
Satan's army lies with the Church.

00:05:04.340 --> 00:05:07.260
Why does no one try to compromise?

00:05:07.470 --> 00:05:09.470
Don't think above your pay grade.

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:16.100
All you have to do is fulfill your duty as bailiff of the Inquisition.

00:05:17.860 --> 00:05:20.570
This is the next list of heretics.

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:35.500
In the end, it was the hero who saved the world, and not us.

00:05:36.580 --> 00:05:40.170
What?! Hushimaen?!
Did you go with Mr. Maou?

00:05:40.380 --> 00:05:41.880
Why'd you leap to that conclusion?

00:05:42.090 --> 00:05:43.300
You didn't?

00:05:43.510 --> 00:05:49.390
Well... I did see him there, but I went with Chiho and Suzuno, not him.

00:05:49.600 --> 00:05:54.560
You keep denying it, but I bet this
Mr. Maou is on your mind, isn't he?

00:05:54.770 --> 00:05:59.860
Frankly, Suzuno's the one most on my mind right now...

00:06:02.820 --> 00:06:04.780
Good after--

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:07.070
Oh, Chi, we've been waiting for you!

00:06:07.280 --> 00:06:10.410
Um, Mr. Maou, what is this?

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:13.160
The landlady sent this stuff from Hawaii!

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:16.540
She told us to sell it in the summer bazaar at the shopping arcade.

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:19.080
I'm sorry, Miss Sasaki...

00:06:19.290 --> 00:06:24.300
I've caused you trouble, all because I'm not... well yet...

00:06:25.720 --> 00:06:26.720
H-Hey!

00:06:26.920 --> 00:06:29.140
Don't knock them around!

00:06:29.340 --> 00:06:31.680
--Are you all right, Mr. Ashiya?!
--I am so ashamed...

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:35.350
--Miss Sasaki, you are so kind...

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:36.520
--Having help is fine, but are you sure this room isn't too small?

00:06:35.350 --> 00:06:36.520
--Live a long life, okay?

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:40.400
--Thank you...

00:06:36.730 --> 00:06:38.600
--What with Emilia here, and all.

00:06:38.600 --> 00:06:40.400
--Emi? How do you know?

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:45.480
--I planted a tracker in her purse a while back.

00:06:40.610 --> 00:06:43.570
--Mr. Ashiya, you mustn't fall asleep!

00:06:43.570 --> 00:06:46.990
--Don't sleep! Don't sleep! Don't sleep...!

00:06:45.490 --> 00:06:46.990
--She'll kill you for that, you know!

00:06:47.190 --> 00:06:49.660
--I'm awake, Miss Sasaki, I swear! You can stop--

00:06:48.150 --> 00:06:50.450
--And what the heck is wrong with her?!

00:06:49.660 --> 00:06:52.160
--Oh, that's good! More!

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:52.160
--We're <i>busy</i>!

00:06:52.370 --> 00:06:53.410
Huh?

00:06:54.370 --> 00:06:56.120
Oh, that room.

00:06:57.960 --> 00:07:03.090
Why should <i>I</i> have to help?
I only came to check on Suzuno!

00:07:03.290 --> 00:07:06.920
Why should I have to get checked on by you?

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:08.760
Can I go home now?

00:07:08.970 --> 00:07:11.390
I'm a NEET, and I have a no-going-outside policy.

00:07:11.590 --> 00:07:15.010
You help too! You're fine if you don't leave the building!

00:07:19.600 --> 00:07:22.860
What kind of taste does the landlady have, anyway?

00:07:23.060 --> 00:07:24.980
Who'd wear a bikini like <i>this</i>?

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:27.610
This one's kind of cute, though!

00:07:27.820 --> 00:07:29.990
Hey, you're right. Maybe I'll buy it!

00:07:30.200 --> 00:07:32.200
--Doubt it'll fit y--
--Shut up, NEET!

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:34.910
There's food, too.

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:40.210
Pineapples, macadamia chocolates, and... Su-pam?

00:07:40.460 --> 00:07:42.920
Oh, and there's juice!

00:07:43.130 --> 00:07:46.420
"Eat the food together," she says.

00:07:46.630 --> 00:07:49.170
"Guava juice"...?

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:50.470
Should we try some?

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:52.640
Oh, I'll go get cups.

00:07:52.840 --> 00:07:54.760
--Do you know where they are?
--I think so.

00:07:56.430 --> 00:07:58.180
I doubt you can uncork it that way.

00:07:58.390 --> 00:08:01.980
Be careful; he's clumsy.

00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:04.610
--Uh... sorry.
--What's wrong with you?!

00:08:04.810 --> 00:08:06.650
Here, wipe up with this!

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:09.440
What's wrong?

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:13.950
Hmm? Oh, it's nothing.

00:08:14.160 --> 00:08:16.240
Um... sorry?

00:08:17.990 --> 00:08:19.830
There were only five.

00:08:20.040 --> 00:08:21.620
Okay, none for Urushihara then.

00:08:21.830 --> 00:08:24.460
Why not?! There are exactly five of us!

00:08:24.670 --> 00:08:28.090
Me, Emi, Suzuno, Chi, and Ashiya.

00:08:28.300 --> 00:08:31.470
--How about you stick to water?
--U-Um, I saw a to-go cup from Sugiya...

00:08:31.670 --> 00:08:34.300
Gah, what the hell?!
Why do you keep doing this?!

00:08:34.510 --> 00:08:37.220
What did I do to deserve this?!

00:08:42.270 --> 00:08:44.100
Thanks, you were a big help.

00:08:44.310 --> 00:08:48.770
It was fun, though. It sort of feels like the day before the Culture Festival!

00:08:48.980 --> 00:08:53.780
Yeah, the prep for a festival gets you more pumped than the real thing, huh?

00:08:53.990 --> 00:08:55.910
What's the matter?

00:08:56.120 --> 00:08:58.490
Oh, I was just thinking that it's been years

00:08:58.700 --> 00:09:02.370
since I've had time to enjoy a festival...

00:09:02.580 --> 00:09:05.790
Then let's all have lots of fun together this year!

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:07.460
With prep <i>and</i> the real thing!

00:09:07.670 --> 00:09:11.340
Well, I'm on shift tonight, so I'm heading to work now.

00:09:11.550 --> 00:09:14.970
Okay, have a good shift!
We'll take care of the rest!

00:09:15.180 --> 00:09:18.930
Sheesh, Chiho, you don't have to spoil the idiot.

00:09:19.930 --> 00:09:22.890
Why do you waste time with silly festival preparations?

00:09:23.100 --> 00:09:28.520
Carry out the objective now, before the Devil regains his magic.

00:09:28.730 --> 00:09:29.770
But...

00:09:29.980 --> 00:09:32.070
Aren't we past the time for hesitation?

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:36.450
You've already stained your hands with blood over and over.

00:09:37.820 --> 00:09:42.120
Curse Saint Aire, getting all high and mighty the moment there's peace...

00:09:42.330 --> 00:09:47.040
They want to keep us away from the rebuilding of the central lands.

00:09:47.250 --> 00:09:49.340
They'll exploit any weakness to come after us!

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:52.590
I can't believe they got hold of an assassinated nobleman's corpse

00:09:52.800 --> 00:09:55.840
and the trial proceedings from the cathedral...

00:09:56.050 --> 00:09:58.180
What has the Prince-Bishopric of Bel been doing?!

00:09:58.390 --> 00:10:03.890
While she may be our lead, handing her over isn't enough to change the situation.

00:10:04.100 --> 00:10:08.270
After all, the Inquisition conducts plenty of unfair trials.

00:10:08.480 --> 00:10:09.980
Then what should we do?

00:10:10.190 --> 00:10:13.230
The hero Emilia, a former
Church knight, and the high priest Olba

00:10:13.440 --> 00:10:16.320
were the ones to defeat the Devil's army.

00:10:16.530 --> 00:10:19.660
Which means that the people owe this peacetime to the Church, doesn't it?

00:10:19.870 --> 00:10:26.710
Just wait! Aren't you the one who made the trials more severe in the first place?

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:29.250
Someone will have to take the blame for that.

00:10:29.460 --> 00:10:30.750
"Blame"? Nonsense!

00:10:30.960 --> 00:10:35.970
The high priest Olba was the one in charge, and he's regrettably missing.

00:10:36.170 --> 00:10:39.550
We have no way of taking responsibility.

00:10:39.760 --> 00:10:40.590
I see.

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:45.020
To avoid delays in trying the heretics while the Grand Inquisitor is gone,

00:10:45.220 --> 00:10:49.020
Father Robertio will establish a "Doctrinal Correction Council"

00:10:49.230 --> 00:10:51.610
and transfer all officers of the Inquisition to it.

00:10:51.810 --> 00:10:55.190
The Inquisition will be suspended until Father Olba returns.

00:10:55.400 --> 00:11:00.200
Under this new leadership, the Council will conduct fairer trials.

00:11:00.410 --> 00:11:04.040
That should be a sufficient story to feed the kingdoms.

00:11:04.240 --> 00:11:08.500
It's always like that.
They don't discipline themselves,

00:11:08.710 --> 00:11:12.040
they fear damage to their institution, they fear being shamed,

00:11:12.250 --> 00:11:16.130
they don't get their own hands dirty, and they steal any glory they can.

00:11:17.380 --> 00:11:21.550
It's not as though I <i>wanted</i> to execute those people!

00:11:21.760 --> 00:11:27.020
I'll say it again: do your job.

00:11:27.220 --> 00:11:29.140
Kill the Devil.

00:11:32.690 --> 00:11:35.730
I shall correct his doctrine.

00:11:55.800 --> 00:11:57.420
Huh...

00:12:01.470 --> 00:12:02.640
Look, Ashiya.

00:12:02.840 --> 00:12:06.640
If you're that sick, go to the hospital!
I'll call for an ambulance!

00:12:06.850 --> 00:12:10.850
We mustn't call--for something so minor--!

00:12:11.060 --> 00:12:15.270
Is that so. Fine, I'll call a <i>private</i> ambulance service.

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:16.650
W-Wait!

00:12:16.860 --> 00:12:19.530
Stop! How much does a private one cost?!

00:12:19.740 --> 00:12:23.070
Will public health insurance cover it?!

00:12:28.700 --> 00:12:29.950
Oh, there she is.

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:32.000
Miss Suzuno!

00:12:32.210 --> 00:12:34.500
What have you been doing?

00:12:34.710 --> 00:12:36.090
Is something wrong?

00:12:36.290 --> 00:12:40.090
No. I was just doing some thinking.

00:12:41.420 --> 00:12:45.510
Oh, Miss Suzuno, how's your job search going?

00:12:45.720 --> 00:12:50.850
If you haven't got one yet, how about coming to our MgR's after all?

00:12:51.060 --> 00:12:53.190
Mr. Maou is there, too, so I'm sure it'll be a comfortable--

00:12:53.390 --> 00:12:55.600
--Good Chiho.
--Yes?

00:12:55.810 --> 00:12:58.690
You shouldn't associate with him any longer.

00:12:58.900 --> 00:12:59.980
Whoa, Suzuno?!

00:13:00.190 --> 00:13:02.490
Emilia, please stay out of this.

00:13:02.700 --> 00:13:06.620
"Emilia"? That's... Miss Yusa's real...

00:13:06.820 --> 00:13:12.790
So you do know about
King Satan. I feared you might.

00:13:13.000 --> 00:13:13.500
Suzuno--

00:13:13.710 --> 00:13:18.130
Emilia. I understand that you have your own agenda here.

00:13:18.340 --> 00:13:21.170
But so do I.

00:13:21.380 --> 00:13:24.180
I realize now that I ought to kill him right away.

00:13:24.380 --> 00:13:27.930
M-Miss Suzuno?! Where is this coming from?

00:13:28.140 --> 00:13:28.970
<i>Kill</i> him--?!

00:13:29.180 --> 00:13:34.390
Do you remember how your MgRonald's was suddenly flooded with people

00:13:34.600 --> 00:13:37.610
as soon as the Devil decorated that Tanabata tree?

00:13:38.610 --> 00:13:41.230
What do you think that means?

00:13:41.440 --> 00:13:42.440
"Means"?

00:13:42.650 --> 00:13:44.530
He used magic.

00:13:46.200 --> 00:13:48.990
Those Tanabata slips were filled with human desires

00:13:49.200 --> 00:13:52.330
and tied to bamboo, which is said to exorcise bad energy.

00:13:52.540 --> 00:13:56.790
Satan subconsciously used them as a medium for spell-casting.

00:13:57.000 --> 00:14:00.210
He only wanted customers to come!

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:03.460
I mean, yes, maybe cheating is bad, but...

00:14:03.670 --> 00:14:05.340
If that were all, it wouldn't be so bad.

00:14:05.550 --> 00:14:09.760
But there's no guarantee he won't start making more dangerous use of his magic.

00:14:09.970 --> 00:14:14.100
Mr. Maou wouldn't do that! That time the alligators escaped into the pool--

00:14:14.310 --> 00:14:18.560
What do you think will happen if the
Devil works his way to the top in Japan,

00:14:18.770 --> 00:14:23.070
becomes trusted and respected, and then betrays this world?

00:14:23.280 --> 00:14:24.150
Not gonna happen.

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:25.320
What?

00:14:25.530 --> 00:14:29.780
No offense, but do you really think getting a promotion at MgRonald's

00:14:29.990 --> 00:14:32.740
makes him capable of world conquest?

00:14:32.950 --> 00:14:37.710
Demons live a long time. We don't know how elaborate his plans are.

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:39.830
We should kill him now, while we can.

00:14:40.040 --> 00:14:40.920
B-But--!

00:14:41.130 --> 00:14:43.170
Perhaps this is painful,

00:14:43.380 --> 00:14:48.220
but you're from entirely different worlds... You shouldn't ever have met.

00:14:48.430 --> 00:14:54.850
I'll erase your memory, and eliminate all traces of Ente Isla in Japan.

00:14:57.270 --> 00:14:58.480
Chiho?

00:14:58.690 --> 00:15:01.520
No... Erase my memory?

00:15:01.730 --> 00:15:04.780
No. You can't do that!

00:15:04.980 --> 00:15:09.410
I don't want to forget.
Not about Mr. Maou, or Miss Yusa,

00:15:09.610 --> 00:15:14.080
or Mr. Ashiya, or you... or I guess even Mr. Urushihara.

00:15:14.950 --> 00:15:20.920
We were lucky enough to become friends, and we had so much fun together...

00:15:21.130 --> 00:15:25.210
And now you want to make me forget all that because it's easier for Ente Isla?

00:15:25.420 --> 00:15:26.630
That's just not fair!

00:15:26.840 --> 00:15:31.510
Good Chiho, taking advantage of your feelings may be part of the Devil's plan.

00:15:31.720 --> 00:15:36.060
To dampen our fighting spirit and make us waver over vanquishing him.

00:15:36.270 --> 00:15:38.600
Mr. Maou isn't like that!

00:15:38.810 --> 00:15:45.360
Why would you say such awful things?
He's working so hard, and he's so nice...

00:15:45.570 --> 00:15:47.740
Why would you...?

00:15:47.940 --> 00:15:49.570
He's the Devil!

00:15:49.780 --> 00:15:53.780
He's the ruler of demons who tormented thousands of humans in Ente Isla!

00:15:53.990 --> 00:15:59.830
So, did you ever <i>meet</i> King Satan before he became Sadao Maou?

00:16:00.040 --> 00:16:00.710
Well...

00:16:00.910 --> 00:16:02.710
You only fought with his army.

00:16:02.920 --> 00:16:06.550
You never even met him in person!
So what would you know?!

00:16:06.750 --> 00:16:11.220
False logic! Obviously a commander bears responsibility for all his troops!

00:16:11.430 --> 00:16:14.720
If he were really thinking stuff that horrible,

00:16:14.930 --> 00:16:18.310
why would he fix the expressway when it got wrecked?!

00:16:18.520 --> 00:16:22.730
He had some ulterior motive!
Something to do with his evil plans!

00:16:22.940 --> 00:16:26.770
What reason is there other than being a nice person?!

00:16:26.980 --> 00:16:31.530
When you cause people trouble, of course you say "I'm sorry"!

00:16:31.740 --> 00:16:35.120
Mr. Maou just did what anyone would do.

00:16:35.320 --> 00:16:39.040
I learned my job from him.

00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:43.960
He carefully taught me things, and when
I messed up he scolded me like he should,

00:16:44.170 --> 00:16:46.790
and he covered for my inexperience.

00:16:47.000 --> 00:16:50.960
Even after he turned into
King Satan, he kept his promise

00:16:51.170 --> 00:16:53.680
to teach me about the ice cream machine!

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:58.310
If a man like that really wanted to take over the world with his demon army,

00:16:58.510 --> 00:17:01.310
then he must've had some reason for it!

00:17:01.520 --> 00:17:05.770
So are you telling us to just forgive and forget?!

00:17:05.980 --> 00:17:08.480
You want us to just pretend the past never happened?!

00:17:08.690 --> 00:17:11.360
Both of you calm down!

00:17:11.570 --> 00:17:13.240
Crestia Bel.

00:17:13.450 --> 00:17:15.660
To be honest, I agree with you.

00:17:15.860 --> 00:17:19.030
--Then join--
--But let me say this one thing:

00:17:19.240 --> 00:17:23.830
the peace I wanted was a world where everyone could be happy.

00:17:24.040 --> 00:17:26.710
I haven't been fighting for a "peace" where we close our eyes

00:17:26.920 --> 00:17:30.500
to the fact that we've made our friends cry.

00:17:30.710 --> 00:17:36.140
I don't intend to let this end with a sacrifice just to get that.

00:17:36.340 --> 00:17:38.640
--Do you really mean that?
--I do.

00:17:38.850 --> 00:17:42.890
You're dreaming. There's no way to do this without paying that price.

00:17:43.100 --> 00:17:44.390
I'll find one.

00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:48.360
Some sacrifices just have to be made!

00:17:48.560 --> 00:17:51.650
But I have to pull it off anyway.

00:17:51.860 --> 00:17:53.780
I'm a hero, after all.

00:17:53.990 --> 00:17:55.450
Miss Yusa...

00:17:59.620 --> 00:18:02.790
Then you have no intention of defeating the Devil.

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:05.500
Not yet, at least.

00:18:05.710 --> 00:18:07.120
I see.

00:18:09.130 --> 00:18:10.710
Miss Suzuno!

00:18:19.970 --> 00:18:26.270
I went a little too far. I hardly know anything about Ente Isla...

00:18:26.480 --> 00:18:28.810
But I said awful things to Miss Suzuno...

00:18:29.020 --> 00:18:33.400
It's fine. We don't choose who we fall in love with.

00:18:33.610 --> 00:18:35.030
Miss Yusa...

00:18:41.160 --> 00:18:42.490
You're the one from--

00:18:43.580 --> 00:18:47.540
I know I asked this before, but why <i>did</i> you choose to attack me

00:18:47.750 --> 00:18:49.830
in such a conspicuous place?

00:18:50.040 --> 00:18:51.540
I can't let this drag on long.

00:18:51.750 --> 00:18:53.460
I'm going to get a little rough!

00:19:01.180 --> 00:19:02.220
Miss Yusa!

00:19:06.140 --> 00:19:07.390
Gotta call Mr. Maou...

00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:09.600
Who <i>are</i> you?

00:19:10.980 --> 00:19:12.690
I warned you, didn't I?

00:19:14.230 --> 00:19:16.900
Men take advantage of women when they're vulnerable.

00:19:17.110 --> 00:19:18.200
You're--

00:19:23.830 --> 00:19:25.040
Mr. Maou, pick up!

00:19:26.620 --> 00:19:27.580
Again?!

00:19:27.790 --> 00:19:32.380
It's no use. This is my power: "Gaze of the Fall."

00:19:32.580 --> 00:19:37.260
It overpowers all users of celestial force, and it belongs to me alone.

00:19:37.460 --> 00:19:39.680
The Fall? Don't tell me you're...?!

00:19:39.880 --> 00:19:45.260
That's right. I've come to release you from your painful mission.

00:19:50.230 --> 00:19:53.310
I'm taking back the Better Half.

00:19:56.020 --> 00:19:57.360
Miss Yusa!

00:20:05.780 --> 00:20:07.660
Miss Yusa!

00:20:07.870 --> 00:20:09.790
Miss Suzuno?

00:20:10.000 --> 00:20:12.460
Are you just like him after all?

00:20:12.670 --> 00:20:15.880
You think Miss Yusa's in the way, just like Mr. Olba did?

00:20:16.090 --> 00:20:19.260
This is just <i>wrong</i>! If Mr. Maou is a demon,

00:20:19.460 --> 00:20:24.180
what does that make <i>you</i> people for betraying the woman who fought for you all?

00:20:27.970 --> 00:20:31.180
Good Chiho... I'm sorry.

00:20:33.100 --> 00:20:35.110
Huh? Chi called?

00:20:36.650 --> 00:20:37.690
Hello?!

00:20:37.900 --> 00:20:40.900
--Hi, this is Chiho Sasaki's mom.
--Huh?!

00:20:41.110 --> 00:20:43.320
Thank you for taking such good care of her.

00:20:43.530 --> 00:20:45.410
O-Oh, you're welcome!

00:20:45.620 --> 00:20:50.500
So... Chiho's not home yet. Is she with you?

00:20:52.500 --> 00:20:57.040
Chiho Sasaki? No clue.
She didn't come back here.

00:20:57.250 --> 00:21:02.340
Anyway, I was investigating that
SFC place, and it smells fishy to me.

00:21:02.550 --> 00:21:03.880
What do you mean?

00:21:04.090 --> 00:21:06.800
You said the manager's name was Mitsuki Sarue, right?

00:21:07.010 --> 00:21:09.350
But that name's not on their employee list.

00:21:09.560 --> 00:21:10.680
Say what?

00:21:10.890 --> 00:21:12.640
Looks like the data's being manipulated.

00:21:12.850 --> 00:21:17.360
You planted a tracker on Emi, right?
Do you know where she is right now?

00:21:17.560 --> 00:21:19.020
Gimme one sec.

00:21:20.900 --> 00:21:25.450
What's with this? She's heading in a straight line, <i>through</i> buildings!

00:21:25.660 --> 00:21:28.080
It's Suzuno, though, not Emilia.

00:21:28.280 --> 00:21:30.490
Where's she headed?

00:21:30.700 --> 00:21:32.040
Maybe the government offices?

00:21:33.660 --> 00:21:36.000
Whoa, Maa, where are you going?!

00:21:37.380 --> 00:21:39.000
I'm coming, Chi!

00:22:18.080 --> 00:22:23.460
<i>Where will morning start from, in this quiet sky?</i>

00:22:23.670 --> 00:22:29.090
<i>Fingertips twining in a pinky</i> <i>swear I pretended not to see</i>

00:22:29.300 --> 00:22:39.300
<i>If the moon's been laughed at,</i> <i>she'll sink away toward yesterday</i>

00:22:39.980 --> 00:22:45.240
<i>Liar, coward--if I'm all these things at once</i>

00:22:45.440 --> 00:22:50.950
<i>Then I only blossomed in dreams</i>

00:22:51.160 --> 00:22:56.500
<i>I hid in the moon's shadow,</i> <i>but the truth is, I was crying</i>

00:22:56.710 --> 00:23:02.210
<i>The tears won't flow anymore--</i> <i>did they all dry up?</i>

00:23:02.420 --> 00:23:08.760
<i>If I could forgive everything,</i> <i>maybe they'd flow again</i>

00:23:08.970 --> 00:23:16.310
<i>But these are all things I want to protect</i>

00:23:37.660 --> 00:23:40.920
"The Devil Carries Out His Duties"
